What are Torrefied Pellets?
Torrefied pellets represent an advanced form of biomass fuel produced through a thermal treatment process called torrefaction. This involves heating biomass materials like wood chips, agricultural residues, or municipal waste in a low-oxygen environment at temperatures between 200-300°C. The process removes moisture and volatile organic compounds, resulting in an energy-dense product with superior combustion properties compared to traditional biomass fuels.
Torrefied pellets offer several advantages:
Higher energy density (up to 25% more than conventional wood pellets)
Improved water resistance and storage stability
Better grindability for co-firing applications
Reduced transport costs due to lower weight
Compatibility with existing coal-fired power infrastructure
These characteristics make torrefied pellets particularly valuable for energy companies transitioning away from coal while maintaining existing infrastructure.
